{"availability":"available","full":"StarKnightt/ocean-drive","name":"ocean-drive","description":"Ocean Drive, Miami Beach at golden-hour sunrise: a photoreal open-world Three.js sandbox in the browser. Walk, drive any car, hit the beach. No install.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":18,"forks":6,"created":"2026-09-27T01:14:21Z","updated":"2026-09-30T19:31:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://starknightt.github.io/ocean-drive/","topics":["3d","blender","browser-game","driving-game","first-person","game-dev","github-pages","javascript","miami","mixamo","ocean-drive","open-world","procedural-generation","sandbox","third-person","threejs","vite","web-audio","webgl","webgl2"],"demo":"https://starknightt.github.io/ocean-drive/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:51.627Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:51.627Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:51.627Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:25:51.627Z","stars":18,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A first-person walk along Ocean Drive in Miami Beach at sunrise, built in Three.js. The sun is a hand's width above the Atlantic, the pastel Art Deco hotels are lit gold, and the palms throw shadows the length of the street. You can walk the sidewalk past the cafés, cross to the park, climb a lifeguard tower and go down to the water, where the swash runs in around your feet. Or get into any car on the street, a parked one or a stopped one in the traffic, and drive it anywhere: down the drive, over the park lawn, down the seawall ramps onto the sand and into the surf. It is a sandbox, not a…","The hotels, the palms, the sand, the ocean, the sky, the signs and every sound are generated in code at load time. The only files the scene loads are the cars, modelled in Blender for this project, the people and their animations from Mixamo, and two Poly Haven CC0 normal maps for the car interiors (see CHANGELOG.md for the provenance). The hotels are invented: there is no real name or brand anywhere in the scene.","The brief it was built from: PROMPT.md. One page, unedited, with a list at the end of where the scene went beyond it."],"features":["It also runs on laptops and phones, on a lower quality tier.","About 22,400 lines of hand-written JavaScript across 57 files in src/.","A district 680 m long, from z −340 to +340, with six cross streets, the park, the promenade","About forty procedural Art Deco hotels: curved bays, eyebrow slabs over the windows, porthole","About 160 palms of three species, coconut, royal and sabal, with fronds that sway in the wind"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/StarKnightt/ocean-drive/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6039dc4178703b151386fe2a594addbc1de86742a1e383a6586f4d0f6cac9a0e","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:51.777Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:51.777Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A first-person walk along Ocean Drive in Miami Beach at sunrise, built in Three.js. The sun is a hand's width above the Atlantic, the pastel Art Deco hotels are lit gold, and the palms throw shadows the length of the street. You can walk the sidewalk past the cafés, cross to the park, climb a lifeguard tower and go down to the water, where the swash runs in around your feet. Or get into any car on the street, a parked one or a stopped one in the traffic, and drive it anywhere: down the drive, over the park lawn, down the seawall ramps onto the sand and into the surf. It is a sandbox, not a…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/StarKnightt/ocean-drive/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6039dc4178703b151386fe2a594addbc1de86742a1e383a6586f4d0f6cac9a0e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/StarKnightt/ocean-drive/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:51.778Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-30T19:31:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/StarKnigh